# 5. Agent 01 — Requirement Intake Specialist

## Responsibility

Retrieve the correct PRD and prepare a normalized requirement package.

## Input

RequirementIntakeRequest

Suggested fields:

- source_type
- source_reference
- session_id
- project_id optional

Example:

{
  "source_type": "confluence",
  "source_reference": "https://...",
  "session_id": "..."
}

## Tools

Confluence MCP only.

Possibly Jira read-only later, but not required for the first implementation.

## Output

RequirementPackage

Suggested structure:

class RequirementPackage(BaseModel):
    requirement_set_id: str
    title: str
    source_type: str
    source_reference: str
    source_version: str | None
    raw_content: str
    retrieved_at: datetime

## Important

The Intake Specialist should do very little reasoning.

Its main job is acquisition and normalization.

Do not make it generate tests.

---

# 6. Agent 02 — Requirement Analysis Specialist

## Responsibility

Convert the PRD into a structured requirement representation.

## Input

RequirementPackage

## Output

StructuredRequirementModel

Suggested models:

class RequirementItem(BaseModel):
    id: str
    title: str
    description: str
    acceptance_criteria: list[str]
    business_rules: list[str]
    dependencies: list[str]
    preconditions: list[str]
    source_reference: str

class RequirementAmbiguity(BaseModel):
    requirement_id: str | None
    description: str
    severity: Literal["LOW", "MEDIUM", "HIGH"]

class StructuredRequirementModel(BaseModel):
    requirement_set_id: str
    title: str
    requirements: list[RequirementItem]
    ambiguities: list[RequirementAmbiguity]
    contradictions: list[str]
    assumptions: list[str]

## Behavior

The specialist should:

- extract functional requirements
- extract acceptance criteria
- identify business rules
- identify dependencies
- identify preconditions
- identify ambiguity
- identify contradictions

It must NOT silently resolve important ambiguity.

If serious ambiguity exists, expose it in structured output.

For v1:

HIGH ambiguity should stop the workflow with:

NEED_HUMAN_REVIEW

Do not yet build the full Human-in-the-Loop UI.

Persist the state and return a clear status so HITL can be added next.

---

# 7. Agent 03 — Test Generation Specialist

## Responsibility

Generate high-quality logical test cases from the StructuredRequirementModel.

This stage is about TEST DESIGN.

It is NOT about automation code.

Do not use Graphify.

Do not generate Python automation.

Do not interact with environments.

## Input

StructuredRequirementModel

Optional:

previous_validation_feedback

## Output

GeneratedTestSuite

Suggested models:

class TestStep(BaseModel):
    order: int
    action: str
    expected_result: str | None

class TestCase(BaseModel):
    test_id: str
    title: str
    objective: str
    requirement_ids: list[str]
    preconditions: list[str]
    test_data: dict | None
    steps: list[TestStep]
    expected_result: str
    test_type: str | None
    priority: str | None
    tags: list[str]

class GeneratedTestSuite(BaseModel):
    suite_id: str
    requirement_set_id: str
    tests: list[TestCase]
    generation_revision: int

## Generation expectations

Tests should include when appropriate:

- happy path
- negative path
- boundary cases
- edge cases
- validation rules
- permission/security-related behavior if specified
- error handling
- state transitions

Do not invent product requirements.

If an assumption is required, mark it.

Maintain traceability:

Requirement ID → Test IDs

---

# 8. Agent 04 — Coverage Validation Specialist

This must be a separate specialist from the Test Generation Specialist.

It acts as an independent reviewer.

## Responsibility

Compare:

StructuredRequirementModel

against:

GeneratedTestSuite

and determine whether the suite adequately covers the requirements.

## Input

- StructuredRequirementModel
- GeneratedTestSuite

## Output

CoverageValidationResult

Suggested models:

class CoverageGap(BaseModel):
    requirement_id: str
    reason: str
    suggested_fix: str

class RequirementCoverage(BaseModel):
    requirement_id: str
    covered_by_test_ids: list[str]
    status: Literal[
        "COVERED",
        "PARTIALLY_COVERED",
        "NOT_COVERED"
    ]

class CoverageValidationResult(BaseModel):
    status: Literal[
        "PASS",
        "REVISE",
        "NEED_HUMAN_REVIEW"
    ]

    requirement_coverage: list[RequirementCoverage]
    gaps: list[CoverageGap]
    unsupported_assumptions: list[str]
    duplicate_or_redundant_tests: list[str]
    feedback: str

## Validation behavior

The specialist must check:

- every requirement has coverage
- acceptance criteria are represented
- expected results are meaningful
- negative paths are included where relevant
- test cases do not contradict the PRD
- unsupported assumptions are detected
- major duplicate tests are detected

If incomplete:

status = REVISE

The feedback is sent back to Test Generation Specialist.

