# 27. Coding Principles

- Prefer simple code over framework magic.
- Do not build abstractions before they are needed.
- Do not introduce a second agent framework.
- Keep LangGraph orchestration explicit.
- Keep Pydantic contracts strict.
- Keep tools small and permissioned.
- Use dependency injection where it improves testing.
- Keep model-specific logic inside the model gateway.
- Keep MCP-specific logic inside adapters.
- Keep Mongo-specific logic inside repositories.
- Make every specialist independently testable.
- Never silently swallow schema failures.
- Never allow unbounded agent loops.
- Prefer deterministic code whenever AI reasoning is unnecessary.

